' Archforge for PlantUML — people and systems
'
' GENERATED and SELF-CONTAINED. Do not edit; edit assets/plantuml/src/ and
' run `node tools/build-plantuml.mjs`.
'
' Include it and nothing else — locally or straight from a URL:
'
'   !include Arch_Context.puml
'   !include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/main/assets/plantuml/Arch_Context.puml
'
' No other files are fetched, no flags are needed, and a fork or a tag
' works without editing anything.
'
' Licence: Apache-2.0.
' Archforge for PlantUML — system context level
'
'   !include https://<you>.github.io/archforge/plantuml/Arch_Context.puml
'
'   Person(customer, "Customer", "Buys things")
'   System(payments, "Payment Platform", "Takes payments")
'   System_Ext(cards, "Card Network", "Authorises cards")
'   Rel(customer, payments, "Pays", "HTTPS")
'
' Licence: Apache-2.0.

' Where the rest of the library is loaded from.
'
' Remote use needs absolute URLs: PlantUML does not resolve a relative
' `!include` against a parent that was itself fetched over http, so a chain of
' relative includes fails as soon as the entry point is a URL. Local use needs
' the opposite. So both are provided, switched by a flag, exactly as
' C4-PlantUML does:
'
'   remote (default)  !include <base>/Arch_Container.puml
'   local             plantuml -DRELATIVE_INCLUDE="." your-diagram.puml
'
' Override the base to point at your own fork or a vendored copy:
'   plantuml -DARCH_INCLUDE_BASE="https://example.com/plantuml" ...
' Archforge for PlantUML — shared foundation
'
' This is the C4-PlantUML-style half of Archforge: a macro library you include
' from a .puml file so you can write C4 diagrams in PlantUML directly, with the
' same palette and structural glyphs the Archforge renderer uses.
'
' You do not need the rest of Archforge to use this. Conversely, if you want
' architecture linting, drift detection against real source code, or the web
' editor, model your system in the .arch DSL instead and use `arch render
' --format puml` to produce PlantUML from it.
'
' Do not include this file directly — include one of the level files, which
' pull this in and add the macros appropriate to that level:
'
'   Arch_Context.puml      people and systems
'   Arch_Container.puml    + containers
'   Arch_Component.puml    + components
'   Arch_Deployment.puml   + deployment and infrastructure nodes
'   Arch_Dynamic.puml      + numbered interactions
'
' Licence: Apache-2.0.

